Iridescent Origins
==================

This product contains software derived from the following upstream projects:

1. Origins (Fabric) -- Copyright (c) Apace100, MIT License.
   https://github.com/apace100/origins-fabric

   The Origins API (power types, layered origin selection, NBT data model)
   was designed and implemented by Apace100 for Fabric. Iridescent Origins
   uses the same power-JSON data model and depends at runtime on the
   Origins Forge port (and the Apoli companion library) which extend
   Apace100's API to the Forge platform.

2. Origins++ -- Copyright (c) MerchantPug, MIT License.
   https://github.com/MerchantPug/Origins-Plus-Plus

   Iridescent Origins was BOOTSTRAPPED by porting the data assets of
   Origins++ (origin definitions, power JSONs, and language entries) into
   the IridescentCraft `icraft` namespace on 2026-03-04 (git commit
   da3e1b36, "Port all Origins++ data to icraft namespace -- remove
   Origins++ dependency"). Origins++ is itself an extension of Apace100's
   Origins. The port allowed IridescentCraft to ship origin content
   without taking Origins++ as a hard dependency.

Significant divergence from upstream (Silvaria, 2026-03-04 onward):

  - Renamespaced every power, origin, and asset key from `origins-plus-plus:*`
    to `icraft:*`. Existing world data referencing the old namespace would
    not migrate.
  - Removed origins / races / classes that didn't fit IridescentCraft's
    design (e.g. Mundane origin, vanilla-only race entries).
  - Added 4 new races (Demi-God, Ryu, Fallen Angel, Kirin) and 10 classes
    (Archmage, Battlemage, Berserker, Samurai, Ranger, Paladin, Vanguard,
    Wanderer, Artificer, Void Summoner) with original power JSONs.
  - Added 4 custom origins (Witch of Ink, Artificial Construct, Witherborn,
    Slimebodied) with original power JSONs and KubeJS progression hooks.
  - Custom Java entrypoint (`IridescentOrigins.java`) registering an Origins
    layer order specific to this pack.
  - Rebalanced ~all retained Origins++ powers (e.g. melee maluses, HP
    modifiers, food-preference tradeoffs) for the IridescentCraft tier
    progression.

The bootstrap of Origins++ data does not imply that this project is
endorsed by or affiliated with MerchantPug or Apace100. The renamespacing
and divergence mean the runtime asset layer no longer overlaps with
Origins++ -- new versions of Origins++ would not conflict with or update
this mod.

